<title>UK: World Bank sets 15 billion yen dual-currency bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank sets 15 billion yen dual-currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following dual-currency bond was announced by joint lead managers LTCB International Ltd and Chase Manhattan International Ltd.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT   *15 BLN YEN    COUPON     5.60	MATURITY    24.APR.00</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL-CURRENCY ISS PRICE  98.50     PAY DATE    24.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.20	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AAA/AAA   DENOMS (K) 500	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> NOTES     *REDEMPTION IN STERLING AT 2,541.29 PER 500,000 YEN</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF GLOBAL MULTICURRENCY NOTE PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
